    "summary": "Stellar Weather Report Suite and soaring Dark Star > Morning Dew",
    "blurb": "The show delivers a powerful Weather Report Suite with horn‑enhanced textures, a thunderous Dark Star that erupts into an unforgettable Morning Dew, and tight transitions like China Cat Sunflower → I Know You Rider. Jerry’s wah‑wah solo in Playing In The Band shines, while Phil’s bass drives the improvisations.",
    "review": "On September 11, 1973 at William & Mary College Hall the Dead rolled out one of their most exciting late‑summer outings. The first set was a roll‑call of classics—The Promised Land, Sugaree, Loser and a seamless China Cat Sunflower → I Know You Rider segue—that set the stage for an electric second half. A horn‑augmented Weather Report Suite (Prelude into Part 1) opened the second set with jazzy flair, leading straight into a thunderous Dark Star where Phil’s bass roared and Jerry’s wah‑wah solo in Playing In The Band cut through the mix. That darkness melted into an epic Morning Dew that built to a cathartic climax before a bright Sugar Magnolia closed the night. Across all recordings the band sounds tight, adventurous, and deeply in sync, making this a must‑listen for anyone chasing that 1973 magic.",
